Set
---
-  Sets are declared by using { }
-  Unordered collection of unique elements
-  In sets we don't have any index number

-Sets are unordered collection of elements
  s1 = {92, 5, 54, 22, 6, 4, 56, 1}
  
  print(s1)
  # {1, 4, 5, 6, 54, 22, 56, 92}

- Sets are always unique data, it never stores duplicates
  s1 = {92, 5, 54, 22, 6, 4, 56, 1, 22, 6}
  
  print(s1)
  # {1, 4, 5, 6, 54, 22, 56, 92}

